  "category": "historical_issue_fix",
  "description": "### Initial Checks\n\n- [x] I confirm that I'm using Pydantic V2\n\n### Description\n\nWe've recently switched the `defer_build` flag to `False` by default in our code base, and have experienced a decent reduction in memory usage and library load time, which is great, since there is a good amount of nested model usage.\n\nHowever a weird issue surfaced: A particular BaseModel in our repo has a field that is defined via NamedTuple, and one of its fields is a BaseModel. For some reason, if the inner model has `defer_build=True` then we get an error:\n```\nError serializing to JSON: TypeError: 'MockValSer' object cannot be converted to 'SchemaSerializer'\n```\nI have managed to simplify to a minimal reproducible example here, and noticed that the issue only surfaced for `NamedTuple` and not regular tuple.\n\n### Example Code\n\n```Python\nimport datetime\nfrom typing import NamedTuple\n\nimport pydantic\nimport pydantic_core\n\nclass LazyBar(pydantic.BaseModel, defer_build=True):\n    x: int\n\nclass Bar(pydantic.BaseModel):\n    x: int\n\nclass EagerNamedTupleFoo(NamedTuple):\n\n    u: float\n    bar: Bar\n\nclass LazyNamedTupleFoo(NamedTuple):\n\n    u: float\n    bar: LazyBar\n\nEagerFooTuple = tuple[float, Bar]\nLazyFooTuple = tuple[float, LazyBar]\n\n\nclass Baz(pydantic.BaseModel, defer_build=False):\n\n    eager_tuple: EagerFooTuple\n    eager_namedtuple: EagerNamedTupleFoo\n    lazy_tuple: LazyFooTuple\n    lazy_namedtuple: LazyNamedTupleFoo\n\n\nfailing_payload = {\n    \"eager_tuple\": [0.0, {\"x\": 2}],\n    \"eager_namedtuple\": [0.0, {\"x\": 2}],\n    \"lazy_tuple\": [0.0, {\"x\": 2}],\n    \"lazy_namedtuple\": [0.0, {\"x\": 2}],\n}\nbaz = Baz.model_validate(failing_payload)\n\nprint(baz.model_dump_json(include=(\"eager_tuple\")))\nprint(baz.model_dump_json(include=(\"eager_namedtuple\")))\nprint(baz.model_dump_json(include=(\"lazy_tuple\")))\ntry:\n    print(baz.model_dump_json(include=(\"lazy_namedtuple\")))\nexcept pydantic_core.PydanticSerializationError as e:\n    # Error serializing to JSON: TypeError: 'MockValSer' object is not an instance of 'SchemaSerializer'\n    print(e)\n```\n\n### Python, Pydantic & OS Version\n\n```Text\npydantic version: 2.13.4\n        pydantic-core version: 2.46.4\n          pydantic-core build: profile=release pgo=false\n               python version: 3.12.3 (main, Jun 19 2026, 12:46:00) [GCC 13.3.0]\n                     platform: Linux-6.6.114.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2-x86_64-with-glibc2.39\n             related packages: typing_extensions-4.15.0 pydantic-extra-types-2.11.1 pydantic-settings-2.14.1\n                       commit: unknown\n```",
